msgid "Extension codestart"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide explains how to create and configure a Quarkus Codestart for an "
"extension."
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"\"Extension Codestarts\" is the name we give to our Quarkus extension "
"\"getting started\" code generation system. It aims to provide a "
"personalized getting started experience with Quarkus.\n"
"A Quarkus extension is able to provide one or more well-defined codestarts "
"which will contain the resources and code required/recommended to start "
"using that particular extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Extension codestarts are applied by default when using the Quarkus tooling "
"(if the chosen extensions contain any):"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://code.quarkus.io[code.quarkus.io, window=\"_blank\"] (find the "
"extensions tagged with [code])"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Quarkus Maven plugin:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Quarkus CLI:"
msgstr ""

msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When starting a project, you choose the language, the build tool, the "
"framework, then you add Dockerfiles, CI, dependencies and code."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Codestarts are working the same way when contributing to the generation of a "
"project, they are split in two categories:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**The \"Base\" codestarts (you choose a combination of those):**"
msgstr ""

msgid "project: The project skeleton (e.g. a Quarkus project)"
msgstr ""

msgid "buildtool: The build tool (e.g. Maven, Gradle, Gradle with Kotlin DSL)"
msgstr ""

msgid "language: The coding language (e.g. Java, Kotlin, Scala)"
msgstr ""

msgid "config: The config type (e.g. yaml, properties)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Extra codestarts (as much as wanted, added on top of the base ones):**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"tooling: Anything that can be added to improve the project (e.g. "
"Dockerfiles, GitHub Actions workflows)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"code: Any Quarkus extension can provide starter code. The user can decide to "
"activate it or not."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each codestart consists of:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A codestart unique name, ie `my-codestart`"
msgstr ""

msgid "A directory for the codestart files, ie `my-codestart/`"
msgstr ""

msgid "A `codestart.yml` file"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally some templates that are following a common structure and naming "
"conventions"
msgstr ""

msgid "Where are the Quarkus Extension Codestarts located"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the Quarkus core repository, the extension codestarts are all in the same "
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/tree/main/devtools/project-core-"
"extension-codestarts/src/main/resources/codestarts/quarkus/extension-"
"codestarts[module, window=\"_blank\"]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus REST (formerly RESTEasy Reactive), RESTEasy and Spring Web extension "
"codestarts are also part of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/tree/main/"
"devtools/project-core-extension-codestarts/src/main/resources/codestarts/"
"quarkus/extension-codestarts[the same module, window=\"_blank\"]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For other extensions, the codestart will typically be located in the runtime "
"module (with special instruction in the `pom.xml` to generate a separate "
"codestart artifact)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Base codestarts"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/tree/main/independent-projects/"
"tools/base-codestarts/src/main/resources/codestarts/quarkus[base codestarts, "
"window=\"_blank\"] contains templates to create project, buildtool, "
"languages, config and tooling files."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In addition, Quarkus also provides the following ways to initialize a new "
"extension project with a Codestart:"
msgstr ""

