msgid "Integration test"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An extension is available to help test extension codestarts "
"`QuarkusCodestartTest`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "It provides a way to test:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the generated project content (with immutable mocked data) using snapshot "
"testing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the generated project build/run (with real data) with helpers to run the "
"build"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extension provides helpers to test that the projects build "
"`buildAllProjects` or just a specific language project "
"`buildProject(Language language)`. It also provides helpers to test the "
"content with <<snapshot-testing>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/main/integration-tests/"
"devtools/src/test/java/io/quarkus/devtools/codestarts/quarkus/"
"ConfigYamlCodestartTest.java[ ConfigYamlCodestartTest, window=\"_blank\"] is "
"a good example in Quarkus core."
msgstr ""

msgid "Snapshot testing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Snapshot testing is a way to make sure the content generated by a test "
"doesn't change from one revision to another, i.e. between commits. That "
"means, the generated content for each commit needs to be immutable and "
"deterministic (this is the reason for using mocked data). To be able to "
"perform such checks, we auto-generate snapshots of the generated content  "
"and commit them as the references of the expected output for subsequent test "
"runs. When the templates change, we also commit the induced snapshots "
"changes. This way, during the review, we can make sure the applied code "
"changes have the expected effects on the generated output."
msgstr ""

msgid "The extension provides helpers to check the content:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`checkGeneratedSource()` validate a class against the snapshots for all "
"languages (or a specific one)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`checkGeneratedTestSource()` validate a test class against the snapshots for "
"all languages (or a specific one)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`assertThatGeneratedFileMatchSnapshot()` check a project file against the "
"snapshot."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can use `AbstractPathAssert.satisfies(checkContains(\"some content\"))` "
"or any Path assert on the return of the methods above to also check the file "
"contains a specific content."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`assertThatGeneratedTreeMatchSnapshots()`  lets you compare the project file "
"structure (tree) for a specific language against its snapshot."
msgstr ""

